WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.731 --> 00:00:06.061
- A lot of people wonder
why I'm living here

00:00:06.061 --> 00:00:08.371
'cause I could live in L.A. or New York

00:00:08.371 --> 00:00:10.760
and be building sculptures there,

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:14.459
but the minute I drive up
to my little ranch here,

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:15.828
I feel like I'm onto something

00:00:15.828 --> 00:00:18.328
that's never been done before.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:26.192
(upbeat music)

00:00:28.439 --> 00:00:29.629
My name is John Lopez,

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.651
and I'm a scrap metal sculptor.

00:00:32.651 --> 00:00:35.234
(upbeat music)

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.253
I use a scoop shovel, I use snow chains,

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.123
I use wrenches, scissors,

00:00:49.011 --> 00:00:51.349
gosh, I use tractor seats,

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:54.516
basically anything that is mild steel.

00:00:56.849 --> 00:01:00.039
(tranquil music)

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:03.869
It just so happens that I
live in a scrap metal paradise

00:01:03.869 --> 00:01:06.229
because every farmer
and rancher in the area

00:01:06.229 --> 00:01:09.901
has a scrap metal pile of some kind.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:12.421
People are very generous around here

00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:15.203
to invite me over and say you can look

00:01:15.203 --> 00:01:16.581
through our scrap pile

00:01:16.581 --> 00:01:18.311
and so, that's where I gather

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.923
my materials for my sculptures.

00:01:20.923 --> 00:01:24.792
So, then I bring all
this found objects home

00:01:24.792 --> 00:01:26.771
that I've hand picked

00:01:26.771 --> 00:01:29.435
and I start grabbing things

00:01:29.435 --> 00:01:31.133
and fitting them up there.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.715
It's a textural experience.

00:01:33.715 --> 00:01:36.363
It's almost like a
patchwork quilt if you will.

00:01:36.363 --> 00:01:38.523
It's got a little bit of everything in it

00:01:38.523 --> 00:01:41.093
and within all that chaos,

00:01:41.093 --> 00:01:44.381
when you step back, the
animal comes to life

00:01:44.381 --> 00:01:47.214
and scrap metal shouldn't do that.

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:53.880
One of the most important things for me

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.832
is to be connected to the land.

00:01:56.832 --> 00:01:59.473
South Dakota inspires me.

00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:03.034
I bought an empty lot
on Main Street in Lemmon

00:02:03.034 --> 00:02:05.942
and right next to the
park that I put it in

00:02:05.942 --> 00:02:08.383
was an old bar called the Kokomo.

00:02:08.383 --> 00:02:10.652
I cleaned the Kokomo out, renovated it

00:02:10.652 --> 00:02:13.383
and turned it into a
really nice art gallery

00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:17.842
where I can feature and
show my finished sculptures.

00:02:17.842 --> 00:02:20.942
I've had people come up to me and express

00:02:20.942 --> 00:02:23.303
in emotion what it means to them

00:02:23.303 --> 00:02:25.314
or I've had letters.

00:02:25.314 --> 00:02:29.554
I've seen a lot of scrap
metal sculptures around

00:02:29.554 --> 00:02:32.922
but I don't think I've
ever seen anybody capture

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:36.023
the life that my sculptures capture

00:02:36.023 --> 00:02:38.522
and maybe it will affect some of the kids

00:02:38.522 --> 00:02:40.103
that live here and their life

00:02:40.103 --> 00:02:41.821
and send them off in a direction

00:02:41.821 --> 00:02:45.238
that it wouldn't if I wasn't living here.

